With $T_0\simeq3\,\mathrm{K}$ and $T_{\rm dec}\sim4\times10^3\,\mathrm{K}$, equation [eq:c07-decoupling-ratio] gives $\boxed{
\frac{a_0}{a_{\rm dec}}
\sim
\frac{T_{\rm dec}}{T_0}
\sim10^3
}.$ Equivalently, the last-scattering redshift is of order $10^3$. Before this epoch the ionized plasma was opaque; after it, photons propagated nearly freely.

