p.src:
Pair reactions change the sum but preserve the difference: $N_{e^-}+N_{e^+}\quad\hbox{changes},
\qquad
N_{e^-}-N_{e^+}=\hbox{constant}.$ In the hot soup $N_{e^-}+N_{e^+}$ is of the same order as $N_\gamma$, whereas the surviving excess is of the same order as the much smaller proton number. Hence the rounded ratio is $\boxed{
\frac{N_{e^-}-N_{e^+}}
{N_{e^-}+N_{e^+}}
\sim10^{-8}
}.$ There was roughly one excess electron for every $10^8$ electron–positron pairs.

